l and anti-inflammatory properties</li>\n<li>Promotes healthy, lustrous hair</li>\n<li>Cures earaches with careful diluted application</li>\n<li>Soothes nausea and stomach discomfort</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>How to Use / How to Apply</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Toothache: </strong>Apply 1 drop on a cotton ball and place directly on the sore tooth for 2–3 minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>Oral hygiene:</strong> Mix 2 drops with toothpaste or tooth powder; brush twice a week.</li>\n<li><strong>Cold/sore throat:</strong> Add 2–3 drops to a bowl of hot water and inhale steam.</li>\n<li><strong>Hair care:</strong> Mix 3 drops in coconut oil, massage scalp, leave for 20 mins, wash off.</li>\n<li><strong>Earache:</strong> Dilute 1 drop in 5 drops of carrier oil; apply gently around (not inside) the ear.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>How It Works</h4>\n<p>Clove oil’s primary active compound is eugenol (72–90% of composition) — a powerful natural anaesthetic and antiseptic. Eugenol temporarily blocks nerve pain transmission, making it one of the fastest natural toothache remedies. It also inhibits the growth of Streptococcus mutans and other oral bacteria responsible for cavities and gum disease.</p>\n<h4>Why Buy From Us?</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Best Seller at Ooty Originals — one of our most reordered products</li>\n<li>High eugenol content — sourced from premium clove buds, not leaves or stems</li>\n<li>Packaged in amber glass to preserve potency</li>\n<li>Trusted by dentists and Ayurvedic practitioners</li>\n<li>Affordable at ₹290 for a 10ml bottle — hundreds of uses per bottle</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Who Can Use This?</h4>\n<p>Adults and teenagers. Widely used by dental professionals, Ayurvedic practitioners, and households as a natural first-aid remedy.</p>\n<h4>Restrictions</h4>\n<p>NOT to be used on pregnant women or newborn babies. Avoid ingestion. Do not apply undiluted on sensitive gums of children.</p>\n<h4>Precautions / Notes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Never apply undiluted clove oil to gums or skin — eugenol can cause irritation.</li>\n<li>Not safe for pregnant women or infants (under 2 years).</li>\n<li>Do not use it in ears without proper dilution — eugenol can irritate ear canals.</li>\n<li>Perform patch test before applying to skin.</li>\n<li>Consult your dentist before using it as a regular dental treatment.</li>\n</ul>','[{\"label\":\"Category\",\"value\":\"Essential Oils\"},{\"label\":\"Packed & shipped from\",\"value\":\"Ooty, The Nilgiris\"},{\"label\":\"Price\",\"value\":\"Inclusive of GST\"}]',NULL,290.00,310.00,40,1,0,0,0,'2026-11-10 10:16:05','2026-11-10 10:16:05'),(46,5,12,'Cypress Oil','cypress-oil',NULL,'Pure Cypress Essential Oil from Ooty Originals — a clinically-studied natural remedy for varicose veins. Improves circulation, reduces vein swelling, and relieves discomfort. Also excellent for aromatherapy and menstrual relief. Available 10ml.','<h4>About This Product</h4>\n<p>Ooty Originals Cypress Oil is derived from the Cupressus sempervirens tree — a powerful essential oil studied for its vasoconstrictor properties, making it one of the most sought-after natural oils for varicose veins, poor circulation, and leg discomfort.</p>\n<p>At Ooty Originals, we bring you the soothing and revitalizing essence of nature through our premium cypress oil, carefully crafted to preserve its purity, aroma, and traditional wellness value. Sourced from quality botanical ingredients and processed with attention to natural integrity, our cypress oil reflects the calm and refreshing character associated with nature-inspired self-care.</p>\n<p>Recognized for its woody, fresh, and balancing aroma, cypress oil has long been appreciated in traditional wellness routines. Many people include this versatile essential oil in massage practices, aromatherapy sessions, and relaxation rituals as part of a balanced lifestyle. At Ooty Originals, we focus on maintaining quality and authenticity so that every bottle delivers a natural experience designed for everyday wellness.</p>\n<p>Often refe